※ pl4g-test: compile=error diag=4535
※ pl4g-test: expect-diag 4535 LANG_REF_NOT_WRITABLE

※ A `mut` field lifts the `mut` its record lacks, and not the one a reference
※ lacks: what a `&` lends is read-only however the record behind it was made,
※ which is what lets several `&` to one place be out at once.

type Counter = mut hits : u8 ; fixed : u8

fn peek(c: &Counter):
    c⌖.hits ← 1u8

let std := ⎕import("std")

@[startup]
fn main(init: std.Init) → u6:
    let c: Counter = Counter(.hits ← 0u8, .fixed ← 7u8)
    peek(&c)
    0u6
